1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Miss Kobayashi, Miss Kobayashi!

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,000
If someone asked, you say I'm the ultimate maid, right?

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,000
No, of course I wouldn't. What are you up to?

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
You're wrong. I think I'm the ultimate maid,

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
and that's the only thing that matters.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
So pretty.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Hold on. Look at this book I found.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
A maid cafe's opening? And it's close, too.

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
It says all who enter will be welcomed by the best maids.

10
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Best maids? But how?

11
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Who do they think they are making such false claims without me?

12
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
That's right. No one should make false claims,

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
including the dragon in front of me currently making them.

14
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Then I'll just turn the cafe to ash,

15
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
and their business will fail as a result of my cursed flame!

16
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Your literal burning love?

17
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
I highly advise against it.

18
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Noted! I'm going to scout out the enemy!

19
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:52,000
I wonder if Toru's okay.

20
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
I've returned from the mortal beyond!

21
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Welcome home. How'd it go? Did you destroy anything?

22
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Of course not! I wound up getting a job there!

23
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
How?

24
00:02:36,977 --> 00:02:40,937
I proudly stormed the enemy's evil den to find their leader.

25
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:42,077
There's an evil den?

26
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:43,197
Fear me!

27
00:02:43,737 --> 00:02:46,237
Oh, are you here to interview for the new maid job?

28
00:02:46,497 --> 00:02:49,137
You're awfully presumptuous wearing a maid outfit already.

29
00:02:49,417 --> 00:02:50,437
You're pretty, though.

30
00:02:51,057 --> 00:02:52,977
And I love your positive attitude.

31
00:02:53,357 --> 00:02:54,237
You were hired.

32
00:02:54,337 --> 00:02:54,757
Yay!

33
00:02:55,577 --> 00:02:57,517
And that's how we returned home victorious.

34
00:02:57,957 --> 00:02:59,857
They call that an interview? They're screwed.

35
00:03:00,277 --> 00:03:03,577
I've had a lot of free time on my hands lately since you and Kana are always out.

36
00:03:03,617 --> 00:03:04,697
I need to fill it somehow.

37
00:03:04,697 --> 00:03:07,497
You're like a bored housewife getting a job for fun.

38
00:03:07,657 --> 00:03:09,377
So you're serious about doing this?

39
00:03:09,817 --> 00:03:10,757
Can you handle it?

40
00:03:11,177 --> 00:03:12,597
What are you talking about?

41
00:03:12,737 --> 00:03:15,637
I gladly work as a maid every day of my life for free.

42
00:03:15,857 --> 00:03:17,197
I'm used to it now.

43
00:03:17,257 --> 00:03:17,637
Don't.

44
00:03:18,057 --> 00:03:20,977
Toru, I may have a job at a bigger company now.

45
00:03:21,277 --> 00:03:23,757
But when I was living with my parents, I worked at a restaurant.

46
00:03:24,317 --> 00:03:27,097
Trust me, don't underestimate the service industry.

47
00:03:27,217 --> 00:03:27,957
Ms. Kapiyoshi!

48
00:03:28,177 --> 00:03:29,217
Don't get me wrong.

49
00:03:29,357 --> 00:03:32,697
Cosplay maids at maid cafes offend me in ways I can't even get into.

50
00:03:32,697 --> 00:03:35,197
But their customer service is worthy of respect.

51
00:03:36,117 --> 00:03:38,117
This is a great opportunity, Toru.

52
00:03:38,257 --> 00:03:40,337
It'll be good for you to learn about the service industry.

53
00:03:40,837 --> 00:03:42,797
You look scary when you point like that.

54
00:03:43,497 --> 00:03:46,117
Well, it's been a while since we had that conversation.

55
00:03:46,417 --> 00:03:48,237
I wonder how Toru's doing at her new job.

56
00:03:48,837 --> 00:03:50,817
Kobayashi, you're a worrywart.

57
00:03:51,277 --> 00:03:51,877
Is this it?

58
00:03:51,877 --> 00:03:54,917
Hello, and welcome home, my master.

59
00:03:55,977 --> 00:03:57,637
And welcome, young lady.

60
00:03:58,717 --> 00:04:01,117
Lots of people dress like Lady Toru.

61
00:04:01,817 --> 00:04:02,937
Interesting design.

62
00:04:03,537 --> 00:04:05,717
Looks like this cafe went with plain style maids.

63
00:04:06,597 --> 00:04:08,957
People don't use the word moe very much anymore,

64
00:04:09,217 --> 00:04:12,037
but they've definitely kept the essence of those times in their theme.

65
00:04:12,517 --> 00:04:13,257
Let's check out the menu.

66
00:04:13,717 --> 00:04:16,177
Oh, this is also true to those roots.

67
00:04:16,177 --> 00:04:18,677
There's a special service with every menu item.

68
00:04:18,777 --> 00:04:20,197
I'm betting the magic chants, like,

69
00:04:20,337 --> 00:04:23,237
filled by tummy with much yummy are different for each as well.

70
00:04:23,397 --> 00:04:24,937
You know a lot, Kobayashi.

71
00:04:25,657 --> 00:04:27,377
I'm gonna tell you a secret, Kana.

72
00:04:27,857 --> 00:04:31,217
One time, long ago, I tried working in a cafe like this.

73
00:04:32,357 --> 00:04:34,597
It didn't work out.

74
00:04:34,917 --> 00:04:36,517
I don't get it, but I'm sorry.

75
00:04:37,077 --> 00:04:38,497
Wait a minute, where's Toru?

76
00:04:38,737 --> 00:04:39,397
Back there.

77
00:04:39,397 --> 00:04:39,997
Hmm?

78
00:04:39,997 --> 00:04:48,737
Table ten, your order's up!

79
00:04:48,877 --> 00:04:49,557
On it!

80
00:04:49,837 --> 00:04:52,157
I'm running low on plates, so let's get some out fast!

81
00:04:52,177 --> 00:04:52,737
Right away!

82
00:04:53,537 --> 00:04:53,797
Hmm?

83
00:04:55,717 --> 00:04:56,077
Hmm?

84
00:04:56,797 --> 00:04:57,117
Hmm?

85
00:05:00,257 --> 00:05:00,697
Ah!

86
00:05:03,697 --> 00:05:04,097
Incredible!

87
00:05:04,697 --> 00:05:05,817
Way to go ahead, Chef!

88
00:05:05,817 --> 00:05:07,897
Thanks for everything you do to help us, Chef!

89
00:05:07,937 --> 00:05:09,077
Chef Toru's the best!

90
00:05:09,177 --> 00:05:09,957
No, thank you!

91
00:05:10,157 --> 00:05:12,757
I'm grateful to have a team who works together so efficiently!

92
00:05:14,457 --> 00:05:15,757
Bye, Ms. Kobayashi!

93
00:05:16,057 --> 00:05:17,277
You came to see me?

94
00:05:17,517 --> 00:05:18,837
Wow, you're doing a great job.

95
00:05:19,037 --> 00:05:20,037
I'm truly surprised.

96
00:05:20,517 --> 00:05:22,097
Told you I was the best!

97
00:05:22,477 --> 00:05:24,637
It's actually been quite easy for me to handle.

98
00:05:25,077 --> 00:05:27,237
I've taken another step forward as a maid.

99
00:05:27,817 --> 00:05:28,537
Except...

100
00:05:29,457 --> 00:05:33,037
I'm not working as a maid at all!

101
00:05:33,317 --> 00:05:34,217
You're a chef.

102
00:05:34,477 --> 00:05:36,537
I'm gonna get someone on the floor to switch with me!

103
00:05:36,857 --> 00:05:38,897
I actually think they put you in the right position.

104
00:05:39,597 --> 00:05:41,697
It's the right position for a volcanic dragon!

105
00:05:43,237 --> 00:05:44,917
Please go out and come back in again!

106
00:05:45,357 --> 00:05:45,777
Huh?

107
00:05:46,177 --> 00:05:47,897
Time to turn delicious now!

108
00:05:47,897 --> 00:05:49,077
It's good!

109
00:05:50,077 --> 00:05:50,597
Greetings!

110
00:05:51,277 --> 00:05:52,197
Welcome, Kobayashi!

111
00:05:52,737 --> 00:05:54,217
You're supposed to say master!

112
00:05:54,477 --> 00:05:57,017
When head chef first started on the floor, she said,

113
00:05:57,397 --> 00:05:59,777
I refuse to call anyone master but Ms. Kobayashi.

114
00:06:00,517 --> 00:06:03,117
That's weird, because she doesn't call me master at home ever.

115
00:06:03,617 --> 00:06:05,997
Will you please have a seat in our comfy booth?

116
00:06:05,997 --> 00:06:07,817
You mean I can finally order something?

117
00:06:09,217 --> 00:06:10,177
Omarice, please.

118
00:06:10,537 --> 00:06:11,717
Kimmy, Omarice.

119
00:06:11,877 --> 00:06:12,197
Okay.

120
00:06:12,537 --> 00:06:13,237
Two Omarices.

121
00:06:13,857 --> 00:06:14,297
Sure!

122
00:06:14,857 --> 00:06:16,137
They'll be out in a flash!

123
00:06:17,097 --> 00:06:19,917
Now I have to perform a spell to make it super delicious!

124
00:06:20,337 --> 00:06:21,237
Make it adorable.

125
00:06:21,797 --> 00:06:22,137
Okay!

126
00:06:22,137 --> 00:06:26,077
I call upon the Shadow King who rules this world!

127
00:06:26,517 --> 00:06:29,077
Make this the greatest it can be with your dark arts!

128
00:06:29,377 --> 00:06:31,777
I beseech thee for quality worthy of praise!

129
00:06:32,437 --> 00:06:35,517
Raise its value and bring forth a monument to your glory!

130
00:06:35,837 --> 00:06:37,697
Let my magic spread and bring corruption!

131
00:06:37,697 --> 00:06:40,897
Let my ideals erode the world and bring mass chaos!

132
00:06:40,897 --> 00:06:44,537
Replace all that is organic with palatable falsehood!

133
00:06:46,537 --> 00:06:48,537
Be ever so delicious!

134
00:06:48,957 --> 00:06:51,237
Mooi, mooi, kyuns!

135
00:06:54,277 --> 00:06:55,777
Yummy to the dummy!

136
00:06:56,497 --> 00:06:57,717
I hope you like it!

137
00:06:57,717 --> 00:07:00,297
He used actual magic, a curse in fact!

138
00:07:00,717 --> 00:07:01,517
So good!

139
00:07:01,537 --> 00:07:02,977
Bring me the head chef!

140
00:07:03,057 --> 00:07:03,937
Hello there!

141
00:07:04,197 --> 00:07:07,677
I am your head chef, maid, and of course dragon,

142
00:07:08,397 --> 00:07:09,677
Tauru the Great!

143
00:07:10,897 --> 00:07:16,057
Okay, she's got talent, but is it enough?

144
00:07:16,777 --> 00:07:19,237
I don't want to be anyone's maid but Ms. Kobayashi,

145
00:07:19,437 --> 00:07:20,297
so I'm gonna quit.

146
00:07:20,537 --> 00:07:21,057
Thank you.

147
00:07:22,017 --> 00:07:23,037
You can't!

148
00:07:23,757 --> 00:07:25,137
Don't do that to us!

149
00:07:25,137 --> 00:07:29,057
Our cafes become famous because of the taste of the recipes you created!

150
00:07:29,337 --> 00:07:32,457
There are so many posts spreading about it online by word of mouth!

151
00:07:32,597 --> 00:07:33,597
Head chef, don't!

152
00:07:33,657 --> 00:07:34,217
Head chef!

153
00:07:35,017 --> 00:07:39,537
Well, maybe I'll teach you the magic chant

154
00:07:39,537 --> 00:07:41,477
so you can make your food delicious after I'm gone!

155
00:07:41,637 --> 00:07:42,277
Make notes!

156
00:07:42,597 --> 00:07:43,937
In order for a human to do it,

157
00:07:44,057 --> 00:07:45,717
first you'll have to draw this magic circle.

158
00:07:49,017 --> 00:07:51,357
Good afternoon and welcome home, my master!

159
00:07:51,697 --> 00:07:53,537
Oh my, what a nice cafe!

160
00:07:54,337 --> 00:07:55,757
We'll take two Oma Rices!

161
00:07:56,117 --> 00:07:57,517
Yes, sir, coming right up!

162
00:07:57,657 --> 00:07:58,297
Here we go!

163
00:07:58,497 --> 00:08:00,357
Now I'll cast a spell to make it delicious!

164
00:08:00,357 --> 00:08:03,877
I call upon the Shadow King that rules this world!

165
00:08:04,297 --> 00:08:06,137
Make this dish the greatest it can be with your dark arts!

166
00:08:06,137 --> 00:08:08,357
I think this is the most unique maid cafe I've ever been to!

167
00:08:08,357 --> 00:08:09,337
Worthy of praise!

168
00:08:09,337 --> 00:08:25,977
I am a maid, not a chef!

169
00:08:26,257 --> 00:08:28,417
Where all the rave reviews about me is a maid!

170
00:08:29,197 --> 00:08:30,997
Give me a favor and spare the mouse.

171
00:08:30,997 --> 00:08:41,617
We predict sudden changes in the weather throughout the day,

172
00:08:41,897 --> 00:08:44,137
so please stay tuned for developing reports.

173
00:08:44,457 --> 00:08:45,717
Next up is the news.

174
00:08:46,297 --> 00:08:48,657
There was a large-scale landslide early this morning.

175
00:08:49,217 --> 00:08:49,617
Whoa.

176
00:08:50,857 --> 00:08:52,837
It looks like part of the Earth was sliced away...

177
00:08:52,837 --> 00:08:54,477
It's the mountain where I met you, Toru.

178
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:55,257
That's weird.

179
00:08:56,037 --> 00:08:58,637
How could they do that to our precious sacred spot?

180
00:08:58,637 --> 00:09:02,277
I'll find the culprit behind this and send them to Jahana and Jahanam!

181
00:09:02,637 --> 00:09:04,737
Then I'll crush their bones and beat them to a man!

182
00:09:04,837 --> 00:09:07,797
But the only ones who could do something like that are...

183
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:09,497
It couldn't possibly be me.

184
00:09:09,677 --> 00:09:12,777
I was reviewing the new parameters for a game event at that time.

185
00:09:13,337 --> 00:09:15,817
Lukawa's been out of the country since yesterday.

186
00:09:16,817 --> 00:09:20,197
And fortunately, I always know where she is because we're bound.

187
00:09:20,497 --> 00:09:21,797
We're bound by magic.

188
00:09:22,077 --> 00:09:23,737
It's so good! Delicious!

189
00:09:24,597 --> 00:09:25,077
Ow!

190
00:09:28,637 --> 00:09:31,097
What the heck are you doing here, Toru?

191
00:09:31,397 --> 00:09:32,217
You're the culprit!

192
00:09:32,557 --> 00:09:33,477
What are you talking about?

193
00:09:33,477 --> 00:09:33,977
The news.

194
00:09:34,237 --> 00:09:35,977
They mentioned a mountain that was damaged.

195
00:09:37,557 --> 00:09:38,197
Oh, yeah!

196
00:09:38,497 --> 00:09:40,297
I was gonna ask you about the same thing!

197
00:09:40,357 --> 00:09:40,497
Huh?

198
00:09:41,137 --> 00:09:42,157
You're saying it wasn't you?

199
00:09:42,577 --> 00:09:44,077
No, I just assumed it was Toru.

200
00:09:44,617 --> 00:09:45,597
Well, it wasn't!

201
00:09:45,697 --> 00:09:46,317
Hold on.

202
00:09:46,537 --> 00:09:49,137
Then that means it had to be some other dragon that we don't know.

203
00:09:49,377 --> 00:09:52,257
There aren't that many dragons powerful enough to break my barrier.

204
00:09:52,937 --> 00:09:54,117
Then who could it be?

205
00:09:54,417 --> 00:09:55,317
It was me!

206
00:09:55,317 --> 00:09:55,877
Ooh!

207
00:10:04,377 --> 00:10:04,937
Hi!

208
00:10:05,097 --> 00:10:05,317
Hi!

209
00:10:07,717 --> 00:10:08,097
Elulu.

210
00:10:10,097 --> 00:10:14,857
What a pretty city this is.

211
00:10:15,237 --> 00:10:17,877
There's chatter and laughter everywhere.

212
00:10:18,697 --> 00:10:22,017
With so many people around, you could be indulging in mass destruction.

213
00:10:22,577 --> 00:10:25,357
Yet here you are, Chaos Dragon, chummy with them.

214
00:10:25,937 --> 00:10:29,197
I was watching because I was a little curious and I see what's going on.

215
00:10:29,657 --> 00:10:30,757
I'm not amused.

216
00:10:31,037 --> 00:10:33,977
What I'm trying to say is, you're an enemy now!

217
00:10:40,977 --> 00:10:41,897
Who is that?

218
00:10:42,277 --> 00:10:42,637
Ilulu.

219
00:10:43,237 --> 00:10:46,517
She's with the most radical wing of the Chaos faction and loves destruction.

220
00:10:47,377 --> 00:10:49,077
I'm sure she followed Toru here.

221
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:50,917
You see what I mean?

222
00:10:50,917 --> 00:10:53,637
She clearly came here to destroy this world.

223
00:10:54,137 --> 00:10:56,957
I see, but I trust that Toru will do something about her.

224
00:10:57,177 --> 00:11:00,617
Miss Kobayashi, Ilulu's might is only slightly below Toru's.

225
00:11:00,917 --> 00:11:03,337
If the two of them fight, they'll destroy this whole region.

226
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:05,197
I'm sure she'll do something about that too.

227
00:11:05,757 --> 00:11:07,357
You really believe in Toru, huh?

228
00:11:07,637 --> 00:11:09,557
Well, it's not like that.

229
00:11:10,117 --> 00:11:13,037
I have no choice, so I'm embracing it.

230
00:11:15,777 --> 00:11:17,657
Destruction isn't permitted in this world.

231
00:11:18,037 --> 00:11:19,157
Yeah, what's your point?

232
00:11:19,157 --> 00:11:21,037
I'm in the Chaos faction too.

233
00:11:21,237 --> 00:11:24,017
If you can't abide by the rules, I'll have to send you home.

234
00:11:24,417 --> 00:11:26,297
I'm more than happy to fight with you.

235
00:11:27,797 --> 00:11:30,077
Attacks like that will have no effect on me.

236
00:11:37,877 --> 00:11:39,017
No, the city!

237
00:11:39,017 --> 00:11:50,517
I can't tell.

238
00:11:50,577 --> 00:11:51,217
Is she struggling?

239
00:11:51,777 --> 00:11:54,857
Toru's trying to protect the city while fighting, so she's at a disadvantage.

240
00:11:56,457 --> 00:11:58,457
Are you saying you're not going to help her?

241
00:11:58,837 --> 00:11:59,577
I can't.

242
00:12:00,117 --> 00:12:01,457
I'm with the Harmony faction.

243
00:12:01,937 --> 00:12:03,657
Normally, Toru and I would be enemies.

244
00:12:03,957 --> 00:12:04,177
Huh?

245
00:12:04,177 --> 00:12:08,437
I've put up a barrier to keep humans away, but that's just to avoid trouble.

246
00:12:09,137 --> 00:12:10,177
What about the others?

247
00:12:10,357 --> 00:12:13,977
If we asked Sir Fafnir, he would say she needs to clean up her own mess.

248
00:12:14,797 --> 00:12:19,877
Lady Lukula is with the Spectator faction, so she doesn't do intervention, and Kana's not strong enough.

249
00:12:20,337 --> 00:12:22,597
If she defeats Toru, I'll be permitted to fight.

250
00:12:23,357 --> 00:12:25,817
Protecting you and the city aligns with the Harmony faction.

251
00:12:25,817 --> 00:12:31,817
But then, she'd be...

252
00:12:31,817 --> 00:12:36,117
What good is believing in her if it doesn't give her strength?

253
00:12:36,357 --> 00:12:38,257
It's the same as observing and doing nothing.

254
00:12:39,117 --> 00:12:41,817
But what else can I...

255
00:12:41,817 --> 00:12:43,177
Elma!

256
00:12:44,597 --> 00:12:45,417
Please don't try.

257
00:12:45,737 --> 00:12:48,177
I know you want me to jump in and help Toru, but I cannot.

258
00:12:48,417 --> 00:12:48,757
Pudding!

259
00:12:49,057 --> 00:12:51,737
I know what you're trying to do, and you can't just buy me...

260
00:12:51,737 --> 00:12:52,377
Cream puffs!

261
00:12:52,777 --> 00:12:53,617
Coffee jelly!

262
00:12:54,177 --> 00:12:55,097
Chocolate cake!

263
00:12:55,097 --> 00:12:56,917
Naples are a pancake!

264
00:12:57,057 --> 00:12:57,377
Ooh!

265
00:12:57,697 --> 00:12:59,797
Anything sweet you can think of!

266
00:12:59,797 --> 00:13:00,417
Ooh!

267
00:13:14,597 --> 00:13:15,277
Ow!

268
00:13:18,517 --> 00:13:21,377
I just hit you with 30 shots of flaming acid.

269
00:13:21,997 --> 00:13:24,757
That's on top of several nice swipes with my claws.

270
00:13:25,097 --> 00:13:26,497
And you gave it an owl?

271
00:13:26,977 --> 00:13:28,057
Then I'm stumped.

272
00:13:28,317 --> 00:13:30,117
I can't think of a solid way to kill you.

273
00:13:30,557 --> 00:13:31,197
Me neither.

274
00:13:31,417 --> 00:13:31,597
Huh?

275
00:13:32,057 --> 00:13:34,857
If I go all out with an attack, the city will be destroyed.

276
00:13:35,237 --> 00:13:37,277
But I know there's no way to defeat you otherwise.

277
00:13:38,157 --> 00:13:41,157
Your attacks are starting to get really annoying as well.

278
00:13:41,697 --> 00:13:42,837
But I can't do it!

279
00:13:42,837 --> 00:13:44,037
I have to protect the city!

280
00:13:44,737 --> 00:13:48,477
I feel like exploding and taking everything with me!

281
00:13:48,977 --> 00:13:49,877
You're bluffing.

282
00:13:49,877 --> 00:13:52,197
Toru!

283
00:13:52,197 --> 00:13:52,557
Toru!

284
00:13:52,877 --> 00:13:54,757
Elmo was awesome and put up a barrier!

285
00:13:55,097 --> 00:13:57,657
Only because Miss Kobayashi decided to bribe me!

286
00:14:00,537 --> 00:14:01,837
That's disgusting.

287
00:14:03,417 --> 00:14:04,517
Relying on humans?

288
00:14:05,157 --> 00:14:06,397
Yeah, well, so what?

289
00:14:06,817 --> 00:14:08,237
We're just getting started!

290
00:14:08,857 --> 00:14:11,437
Now to destroy this world with my trauma!

291
00:14:11,437 --> 00:14:35,377
That was a close call.

292
00:14:35,377 --> 00:14:37,817
I didn't take much damage.

293
00:14:38,637 --> 00:14:41,697
But I nearly forgot I had to protect the city, too.

294
00:14:43,077 --> 00:14:46,397
For a moment, I thought about letting everyone else in this world die.

295
00:14:47,037 --> 00:14:48,457
Except Miss Kobayashi.

296
00:14:49,157 --> 00:14:51,577
But then I wouldn't be able to stay here with her.

297
00:14:54,697 --> 00:14:55,377
Miss Kobayashi...

298
00:14:55,377 --> 00:15:02,117
I am...

299
00:15:02,117 --> 00:15:11,297
Wanna go home?

300
00:15:11,657 --> 00:15:12,477
Hmm...

301
00:15:12,477 --> 00:15:15,657
Yeah...

302
00:15:15,657 --> 00:15:21,037
I will fight as hard as I must.

303
00:15:21,037 --> 00:15:27,137
If it means staying with Miss Kobayashi, I can destroy any obstacles that stand in my way.

304
00:15:36,717 --> 00:15:38,317
That human back there.

305
00:15:39,017 --> 00:15:42,037
She got Elma involved and saved Toru.

306
00:15:42,937 --> 00:15:44,057
Humans are our enemies.

307
00:15:44,057 --> 00:15:50,197
That's what we were taught, but there's something about that one.

308
00:15:50,897 --> 00:15:52,077
I want to know more.

309
00:15:57,357 --> 00:15:58,997
Me? Me who?

310
00:15:59,537 --> 00:16:00,217
Oh, yeah.

311
00:16:00,857 --> 00:16:01,197
Oh.

312
00:16:02,137 --> 00:16:04,157
A cold, huh?

313
00:16:05,077 --> 00:16:06,037
On the train?

314
00:16:06,437 --> 00:16:07,437
Your bag?

315
00:16:07,437 --> 00:16:07,997
Hmm.

316
00:16:11,617 --> 00:16:12,297
Compensation?

317
00:16:12,297 --> 00:16:13,477
By today?

318
00:16:13,777 --> 00:16:14,437
Two million?

319
00:16:20,437 --> 00:16:22,077
Oh, that's terrible.

320
00:16:22,077 --> 00:16:37,017
It was harder to get that gate open than I expected.

321
00:16:37,537 --> 00:16:40,697
I'm surprised Toru could easily pull off something so draining.

322
00:16:40,697 --> 00:16:44,377
The last train.

323
00:16:44,717 --> 00:16:48,197
I guess I could have Toru come pick me up instead, but she's probably tired.

324
00:16:48,417 --> 00:16:49,037
Or...

325
00:16:49,037 --> 00:16:50,217
It's you.

326
00:16:50,477 --> 00:16:51,957
The human called Kobayashi.

327
00:16:52,497 --> 00:16:54,717
I want to know why you choose to live with a dragon.

328
00:16:55,577 --> 00:16:58,217
Because Toru decided she wanted to stay in my life.

329
00:16:58,377 --> 00:16:59,917
Believe me, I didn't try to convince her.

330
00:17:00,757 --> 00:17:01,657
Aren't you afraid?

331
00:17:02,517 --> 00:17:03,377
Hear me, human!

332
00:17:03,377 --> 00:17:06,777
Hard to be afraid of her when she's so cute most of the time.

333
00:17:07,377 --> 00:17:07,697
Oh.

334
00:17:09,917 --> 00:17:11,237
So she turns you on?

335
00:17:11,597 --> 00:17:11,797
Oh.

336
00:17:12,157 --> 00:17:15,977
The reason you're not afraid of Toru in her human form is because you're in love with her.

337
00:17:16,577 --> 00:17:16,877
Huh?

338
00:17:16,877 --> 00:17:18,957
Of course not!

339
00:17:19,097 --> 00:17:20,157
What are you talking about?

340
00:17:20,397 --> 00:17:21,777
What a powerful denial.

341
00:17:22,217 --> 00:17:22,737
Suspicious.

342
00:17:22,937 --> 00:17:23,817
That's not it!

343
00:17:24,477 --> 00:17:24,877
Then...

344
00:17:24,877 --> 00:17:30,817
What is this?

345
00:17:31,037 --> 00:17:31,477
Wow.

346
00:17:32,257 --> 00:17:34,997
Well, you're only human in the end, right?

347
00:17:35,237 --> 00:17:36,737
You can't resist your desires.

348
00:17:37,097 --> 00:17:41,157
Go ahead and let your pitiful male instincts run wild and free for once.

349
00:17:41,497 --> 00:17:42,797
You want to be loved, don't you?

350
00:17:42,897 --> 00:17:45,737
Tonight you can finally unleash your lustful longings.

351
00:17:45,957 --> 00:17:46,437
Go on.

352
00:17:46,617 --> 00:17:47,297
Do it!

353
00:17:47,477 --> 00:17:48,097
Do it!

354
00:17:48,617 --> 00:17:50,257
Get your kicks out of my face!

355
00:17:50,337 --> 00:17:50,837
I'm a woman!

356
00:17:51,557 --> 00:17:52,817
Cut the crap, okay?

357
00:17:52,817 --> 00:17:57,597
Wait, those lumps of flesh do nothing but unleash flames of rage and resentment any time I see them!

358
00:17:58,137 --> 00:17:58,977
Oh, no!

359
00:17:59,077 --> 00:18:00,377
The last train's about to leave!

360
00:18:00,517 --> 00:18:00,817
Wait!

361
00:18:00,917 --> 00:18:01,457
Come back!

362
00:18:03,557 --> 00:18:06,677
Please do not rush to board the train while doors are closing.

363
00:18:16,937 --> 00:18:17,917
Well, what?

364
00:18:18,177 --> 00:18:19,717
Haven't you caused enough commotion?

365
00:18:20,857 --> 00:18:21,257
Mm-hmm.

366
00:18:22,817 --> 00:18:24,557
I cannot accept you.

367
00:18:24,797 --> 00:18:25,057
Huh?

368
00:18:25,677 --> 00:18:28,297
Humans and dragons are never permitted to coexist.

369
00:18:29,257 --> 00:18:29,637
Hmm.

370
00:18:30,277 --> 00:18:32,457
When together, their differences cause suffering.

371
00:18:33,017 --> 00:18:35,117
As that suffering grows, it breeds hatred.

372
00:18:35,957 --> 00:18:37,137
Respect turns to envy.

373
00:18:37,717 --> 00:18:39,397
And eventually creates pain.

374
00:18:40,857 --> 00:18:43,597
What Toru feels for you is not what you think.

375
00:18:43,957 --> 00:18:45,237
It's simply curiosity.

376
00:18:45,237 --> 00:18:49,017
And when that eventually runs out...

377
00:18:49,017 --> 00:18:51,377
Wake up!

378
00:18:53,177 --> 00:18:53,957
Everything's fine.

379
00:18:54,037 --> 00:18:55,417
I was listening, I promise.

380
00:18:55,777 --> 00:18:56,417
You liar!

381
00:18:56,697 --> 00:18:59,517
You were talking about the differences between species or something.

382
00:18:59,897 --> 00:19:01,897
You can't accept me and we shouldn't coexist.

383
00:19:02,717 --> 00:19:06,197
So is there anything a lowly human like myself can do to help you?

384
00:19:06,457 --> 00:19:07,697
Correct your understanding!

385
00:19:08,237 --> 00:19:08,797
Hmm.

386
00:19:08,797 --> 00:19:14,777
Then please allow me to borrow your own words to make an important point.

387
00:19:15,777 --> 00:19:19,937
When we embrace our differences and learn to enjoy them, it breeds love.

388
00:19:20,457 --> 00:19:23,577
Respect is joined by trust and eventually creates a bond.

389
00:19:23,577 --> 00:19:28,797
I never thought I would ever say that about my life with Toru, but it's completely true.

390
00:19:29,177 --> 00:19:30,917
That's just a convenient interpretation.

391
00:19:31,177 --> 00:19:32,497
There are still tragedies, too.

392
00:19:32,797 --> 00:19:35,177
You're glossing over the truth with a bunch of pretty words.

393
00:19:36,297 --> 00:19:37,217
Yeah, you're right.

394
00:19:37,697 --> 00:19:37,977
Huh?

395
00:19:37,977 --> 00:19:42,097
There are times we fight and hurt each other, but I try not to think about it too much.

396
00:19:42,697 --> 00:19:45,937
Some might say I'm repressing anger, but I call it choosing battles.

397
00:19:46,937 --> 00:19:51,057
Even if I don't always understand her feelings, I do what I can to respect them.

398
00:19:51,457 --> 00:19:52,097
And we manage.

399
00:19:52,897 --> 00:19:54,297
I guess it's just the way I am.

400
00:19:54,997 --> 00:19:56,777
Is that how you humans really think?

401
00:19:57,117 --> 00:20:00,137
No, but it is the way that I personally think.

402
00:20:01,297 --> 00:20:05,037
Wouldn't you agree that there's a distinction between the way you and other dragons in your

403
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:05,877
realm see things?

404
00:20:05,877 --> 00:20:08,177
No, but there's no need to.

405
00:20:08,617 --> 00:20:09,457
We're the same.

406
00:20:10,017 --> 00:20:10,397
Really?

407
00:20:10,717 --> 00:20:14,757
But what about the dragon who came up with these absolute guidelines for how a dragon should

408
00:20:14,757 --> 00:20:15,077
think?

409
00:20:15,777 --> 00:20:17,217
It wasn't you, was it?

410
00:20:17,217 --> 00:20:39,257
You can spout pretty words, but you're still a human.

411
00:20:39,257 --> 00:20:41,777
It didn't work because you're a female.

412
00:20:48,997 --> 00:20:49,757
Whoa!

413
00:20:52,437 --> 00:20:54,337
I guess the Lulu left?

414
00:21:00,677 --> 00:21:01,397
Huh?

415
00:21:01,397 --> 00:21:05,137
You got to be kidding me.

416
00:21:05,137 --> 00:21:05,957
You got to be kidding me.

417
00:21:06,137 --> 00:21:07,277
Hmm?

418
00:21:18,137 --> 00:21:19,617
Hmm?

419
00:21:24,257 --> 00:21:25,997
Hmm?

420
00:21:25,997 --> 00:21:26,997
Hmm?

421
00:21:26,997 --> 00:21:27,997
Hmm?

422
00:21:27,997 --> 00:21:28,997
Hmm?

423
00:21:28,997 --> 00:21:30,997
Is that good?

424
00:21:30,997 --> 00:21:31,997
Ah!

425
00:21:31,997 --> 00:21:32,997
The fate of mankind!

426
00:21:32,997 --> 00:21:35,997
It's in jeopardy!

427
00:23:19,887 --> 00:23:25,127
Ms. Kobayashi, aren't you excited?

428
00:23:25,467 --> 00:23:27,987
The love story of me and you is finally continuing!

429
00:23:28,407 --> 00:23:30,207
Is it? Wasn't there a new dragon?

430
00:23:30,467 --> 00:23:31,727
She won't show up anymore.

431
00:23:31,867 --> 00:23:32,707
That's not true.

432
00:23:35,447 --> 00:23:37,987
This week on Who's Rotten?

433
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:39,147
Leo.

